      "slug": "timekeeping-support-and-overtime",
      "title": "Actual time, support activities and corrections",
      "bodyHtml": "<p>The Workplace Handbook identifies activities eligible for indirect pay and support-activity pay. These activity types will be added to the web application as needed. ITSCO reserves the right to designate activities as indirect work or support activities and to add, revise or reclassify activity types prospectively. The applicable classification and rate will be communicated before the work is performed. Record actual compensable time under the designated activity; a missing app option should be reported for entry or correction. A later classification change does not reduce pay already earned or permit duplicate payment.</p><p>Record all compensable work daily. Provider Update active review time is tracked by session and section and submitted for payroll review at the applicable support activity rate. Paused, hidden and timed-out periods are not automatically credited; report legitimate unrecorded work through a correction request. Actual work beyond an allowance remains compensable.</p><p>Clinical credits and automatic indirect equivalents are not substitutes for actual time records. Apply applicable minimum wage, overtime, rest-period and regular-rate rules, including workweek and daily requirements. A late note, missing preapproval or denied claim does not erase earned wages. Handle documentation or approval concerns separately from paying for work performed.</p><!-- supervisor-compensation-october-2026 --><h3>Clinical supervision compensation</h3><p>Clinical supervision is paid at the supervisor’s individually negotiated or contracted hourly rate. This handbook does not set a universal supervision dollar rate.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Assigned responsibility</th><th>Compensation basis</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Direct clinical supervision</td><td>100% of the contracted supervision hourly rate</td></tr><tr><td>Hosting group clinical supervision</td><td>150% of the contracted supervision hourly rate</td></tr><tr><td>Reviewing and co-signing another provider’s notes</td><td>50% of the contracted supervision hourly rate per actual note-review hour</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Group pay is based on actual hosting time, not the number of participants. Note-review pay covers actual time reviewing and co-signing another provider’s notes, not the supervisor’s own notes. Record review time separately without duplicate payment or an automatic allowance per supervision hour. Paused and inactive time is excluded from automatic tracking; report legitimate work the tracker misses for correction. Tracked time remains under payroll review until accepted and applied. The supervisor’s individual agreement identifies their contracted rate.</p>\n<h4>Outreach event work and travel</h4><p>Clock in and out for actual assigned outreach event work at your applicable indirect rate. Record travel and materials handling separately, without duplicating event work time.</p><p>For an assigned outreach event, use <strong>Submit → Payroll &amp; reimbursements → Event travel reimbursement</strong> for trips to and from the event and related materials pickup or return. One report covers eligible travel and materials-handling time at the employee's Support Activity rate and eligible personal-vehicle mileage at the applicable event mileage rate. Payroll reviews the actual trips and the policy or agreement in effect when they occurred. Follow the <a href=\"https://app.itsco.health/itsco/workplace-handbook#handbook-event-travel-reimbursement\">Outreach travel reimbursement</a> policy; do not submit separate mileage or Support Activity travel claims for the same outreach assignment.</p>"
