    {
      "slug": "training-leave-benefit",
      "title": "Training leave — separate from sick leave",
      "bodyHtml": "<p>Training PTO is paid time earned for approved professional development and training. All hours and service-credit equivalents that qualify for sick-leave accrual also qualify for training accrual, including fee-for-service and salaried employees’ eligible work. The rate is <strong>0.25 training hour per 30 qualifying hours or credits</strong>. Use the same documented qualifying basis as sick leave, including applicable clinical-credit equivalents; do not add an equivalent twice.</p><p>Training PTO is restricted to approved training and may not be converted to general PTO. It pays at the employee’s applicable sick-leave payment rate for the use date. Required employer training remains paid work even if this benefit has no available balance.</p><h2>Tracking, cap and ADP handoff</h2><p>People Operations enters or confirms the current ADP training balance in the app, together with the last completed pay period included in that balance. The app then accrues subsequent eligible periods without counting imported hours again. Staff view their balance and requests in My Payroll. Unused training hours carry forward until used. Accrual pauses at a <strong>20-hour balance cap</strong> and resumes after approved use; a cap does not erase an existing balance.</p><h2>Requesting Training PTO</h2><p>In My Payroll, choose Training PTO, enter the training date and hours, provide a brief description, enter the training cost and upload a receipt, signup confirmation or proof of participation. People Operations may request further participation documentation. ITSCO may deny a request if sufficient documentation is not provided. The balance is deducted only when payroll approves the request and applies its payment. Pending or denied requests do not reduce the earned balance. A separate expense reimbursement requires its own approval; reporting a course cost does not automatically create a second payment.</p><p>See Continuing Education in the Employee Benefits Overview for additional approval and reimbursement requirements. Training leave is separate from protected sick leave and school support activity hours.</p>"
    },
    {
      "slug": "compensation-regardless-of-funding-source",
      "title": "Consistent compensation across funding sources",
      "bodyHtml": "<p>Beginning on this amendment’s effective date, I will be compensated at the applicable rates in my individual compensation schedule for the services and duties I perform, regardless of the payment or funding source. This includes insurance, self-pay, grants, iMatter and other externally funded programs or contracts. My compensation is based on the approved service, credits or hours and assigned duties, rather than a percentage of the amount billed, collected or reimbursed. For work covered by this amendment, these terms replace prior funding-specific percentage or revenue-sharing compensation arrangements. Applicable approved differentials and separately stated role or duty rates continue to apply. This change applies prospectively after the required signatures and does not reduce compensation already earned.</p><h2>Rationale</h2><p>Funding arrangements have changed over time, and some external contracts have omitted provider-compensation terms or applied them inconsistently. Using each employee’s agreed service and duty rates provides a consistent basis for compensation across programs. Differences in a program’s reimbursement do not create an automatic increase or decrease in the employee’s rate.</p><p>For example, a covered 1.00-credit clinical service pays the employee’s agreed per-credit rate whether funded by insurance, a grant or iMatter. It is not paid as 50% of a program’s reimbursement under this amendment. Salaried employees remain subject to their salary agreements. Approved supervision, mentoring and other assigned-duty rates remain governed by the employee’s individual schedule. Any separate group-work compensation must be agreed in writing under the group-review policy.</p><p>Payroll must retain the prior arrangement for earlier service dates and apply the new method only from the completed amendment’s prospective effective date. Editing the handbook alone does not change an existing signed agreement or activate a percentage-pay override.</p>"
    },
    {
      "slug": "health-insurance-employee-only-contribution",
      "title": "Health Insurance — employee-only employer contribution",
      "bodyHtml": "<h2>Basis of the agency contribution</h2><p>For eligible employees enrolled in agency-sponsored health insurance, the agency contribution is based on the premium for employee-only coverage and the contribution percentage or amount applicable to the employee’s benefit eligibility. Enrollment in employee-plus-spouse, employee-plus-child or family coverage does not increase the agency contribution. The agency does not contribute toward the additional cost of dependent coverage.</p><h2>Employee responsibility and dependent enrollment</h2><p>The employee pays the portion of the employee-only premium not covered by the agency contribution, plus the full additional premium for enrolled dependents. Eligible dependents may still enroll when permitted by the plan; this policy limits the agency’s premium contribution and does not exclude dependents from coverage. It does not promise payment of the employee’s full premium.</p><h2>Where to review your benefit</h2><p>Review My Benefits → Health Insurance in the app for enrollment information, the applicable employer contribution and benefit eligibility. People Operations maintains the employee-only premium used to calculate the contribution, separately from any additional dependent premium. Contact People Operations if the displayed premium includes family coverage or differs from the carrier’s employee-only amount.</p><p>The governing plan documents and applicable law control coverage, eligibility, enrollment and administration. Any change affecting an existing contribution arrangement must be applied prospectively with required notice and any required agreement; this handbook update does not itself change payroll deductions or an existing signed agreement.</p>"
    }
